Executive Summary

Maternal and Perinatal Death Surveillance and Response (MPMSR) is a critical quality improvement system aimed at identifying, reviewing, and preventing avoidable maternal and perinatal deaths—including stillbirths—by understanding causes, delays, and health system gaps. It uses continuous cycles of data collection, analysis, recommendations, and follow-up actions to improve care quality and prevent future deaths. MPMSR has led to improved data collection, accountability, quality healthcare improvements, and community engagement. Key features include mandatory reporting, no-blame culture, confidentiality, and continuous quality improvement. The system relies on identifying deaths and gaps in services provision, determining causes, assigning preventive measures, and following up to ensure implementation.

